  "note": "Complete individual U-shaped principal Rundāle Palace, including rear range, two long side wings, both returned front wings, one open court/gate gap, attached raised center attic/pediment, hipped sheet-metal roofs with round dormers/large chimneys, raised entrances/central and side court stairs and paired gate posts/grilles. Independent curved outbuildings, gardens and access roads remain context. Original picture-guided relative heights on an approximate23m reference from two unmodified standard viewer Terrariumtiles. Court paving23.8m,raised first-floor entrances26.4m,eave37.5m andcentral attic roof44.6m are visualization levels,not surveyed measurements. Fine ornament/inventories and historic grades remain approximate. +X NNE north court gate and detached outbuildings; -X SSW rear garden facade; +Z ESE east wing; -Z WNW west wing. +Y up. Internal architectural u=east/v=south can map to model[-v,u]. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
